 "_about": "Joconde 'Sujet représenté' terms -> taxonomy theme ids (or ic:<Iconclass notation>). Terms are the items inside 'category (term, term)'; matching ignores case; accented source terms must match exactly (châsse, a reliquary, is not chasse, a hunt). 'any' terms count in every category; 'figure' terms only in single-figure religious categories (a 'Christ' inside a biblical scene is not a devotional image); 'animal' terms only outside biblical and mythological categories (the eagle of St John is not an eagle theme); 'landscape' terms only in landscape categories; 'allegory' terms (seasons, virtues, senses...) only in allegorical and single-figure categories (a winter landscape is not the personified Winter); portrait categories are skipped (a sitter called César or Hélène is not a subject). 'fallback' gives a category its broad code when none of its terms map. Reviewed 2026-11-05 against the full term frequency list.",
